        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ion Luca Caragiale, Ion Creangă\n- Roles: playwright, short story writer, poet, theater manager, political commentator, journalist, writer, raconteur, schoolteacher\n- Places: Wallachia, Romania, Moldavia\n\nFacts:\n- Ion Creangă was born on March 1, 1837, and was also known as Nică al lui Ștefan a Petrei, Ion Torcălău, and Ioan Ștefănescu.\n- Ion Creangă was Moldavian and later Romanian, and he worked as a writer, raconteur, and schoolteacher.\n- Ion Luca Caragiale was born on February 13, 1852, with an Old Style birth date of February 1, 1852, and was commonly referred to as I. L. Caragiale.\n- Ion Luca Caragiale was Wallachian and later Romanian, and he worked as a playwright, short story writer, poet, theater manager, political commentator, and journalist.\n- Ion Creangă died on December 31, 1889.\n- Ion Luca Caragiale died on July 9, 1912.",
